  "GENERIC default profile (review R1 item 3): ONE stock optics asset serves every film curve today, so nothing here may claim to be the measured optics of the material being rendered. Blocks whose numbers come from Kodak 5207 measurements carry provenance `derived` — measured amplitude, generic binding; per-curve binding (true measured for vision3250d, PGI-scaled or own-scan for Portra/Ektar/Velvia) is the recorded follow-up.",
  "halation: the 35mm_strong_ah_modelled component set (modelled; P2 geometry, dc_mode residual — the characteristic curve already holds the uniform-field reflection).",
  "grain (V2 P4): sigma(D) amplitude digitized from H-1-5207 (measured source), field geometry pitch/size/layer_corr and the particle-oracle band mixture are modelled — hence `derived` overall. The dye-amount coordinate is treated as net Status-family density (R1 item 1); the residual densitometer crosstalk is not modelled.",
  "emulsion_scatter (V2 P5): kernel fitted from the H-1-5207 MTF chart (measured source, fitted approximation -> `derived`); engages with the spatial context as a medium property."
